Yes—assuming you mean **I2P+** (I2P Plus). It’s a community-maintained fork of the Java I2P router, focused on router performance and a more approachable console, while remaining compatible with the I2P network. The I2P project lists it as an actively maintained alternative client. [I2P+ project](https://i2pplus.github.io/) · [I2P alternative clients](https://i2p.net/en/docs/overview/alternative-clients/) · [I2P+ source](https://github.com/I2PPlus/i2pplus/)

I understand “pre-wired” as making I2P+ work smoothly with Synapse’s main I2P browsing mode: clear setup and connection status, a dedicated I2P profile alongside regular profiles, and launching through the I2P+ proxy only when the router is actually ready. I’d preserve the important caveat that I2P+ may route clearnet sites through its configured outproxy, so Synapse should make that policy visible rather than implying every request stays on I2P. No code has been changed for this yet.

