You’re right to ask for something concrete. I’ve changed I2P mode so the dedicated profile opens the local I2P+ Router Console on startup, where its curated starter links are available once the router is bootstrapped. The I2P launcher also has an **Address Book** button that opens SusiDNS subscriptions. The I2P+ hosts feed is shown as optional—not silently added—because subscribing is a trust decision.

I also made the regular Synapse launcher block I2P startup unless the local proxy is listening, and added tests for the start page and allowed console route. The changes are in [the I2P mode UI](src/control/i2p_mode.ks), [I2P routing helpers](src/core/i2p.k), and the [I2P documentation](README.md#L128).

**Verification:** core contracts passed, and the controller and tool sources compiled with the local Krypton compiler. I didn’t run the Windows browser or test the flow against a live I2P+ router here. The address-book feed URL is `http://skank.i2p/hosts.txt`; Synapse does not subscribe to it automatically.
