I added a **macOS I2P+ development path** to the existing controller. It checks for the local proxy at `127.0.0.1:4444`, creates a persistent I2P profile separate from Shield for each supported identity, applies the I2P startup preferences, and launches Synapse at the local Router Console. You can also open SusiDNS directly:

```bash
tools/synapse-macos.sh i2p-check
tools/synapse-macos.sh i2p-open personal
tools/synapse-macos.sh i2p-open personal subscriptions
```

The optional `http://skank.i2p/hosts.txt` address-book feed is **not** added automatically. I documented the macOS path in the [README](README.md#L160), updated the [privacy notes](docs/PRIVACY.md#L58) and [roadmap](docs/ROADMAP.md#L61), and left the unrelated `.DS_Store` changes untouched. Existing Windows-related edits remain in the working tree; Windows testing is still deferred.

**Checks passed:** core contracts, shell syntax, and Krypton compiler checks for the controller and tool. I also verified that the proxy check rejects an absent listener and accepts a test listener. I2P+ itself is not running, so a real browser-to-router launch remains unverified. Once that baseline is confirmed with I2P+ on macOS, we can redesign the UI.
