I’ve built the first usable macOS I2P control panel: **Synapse Settings · I2P Network**. It has router status, explicit start and graceful-stop actions, browser identity selection, Open I2P Browser, and Address Book. Automatic startup is shown as off.

Open it with:

```bash
tools/synapse-macos.sh i2p-settings
```

The panel and launcher are in [src/control/i2p_settings.ks](src/control/i2p_settings.ks) and [tools/synapse-macos.sh](tools/synapse-macos.sh). I updated the [macOS instructions](README.md#L160) and [roadmap](docs/ROADMAP.md#L65). The app compiled and stayed running; shell syntax, core contracts, and diff checks passed.

**This is a standalone macOS settings window, not yet a page inside Firefox’s Settings.** It manages an existing I2P+ installation; it does not install or bundle the router, and I couldn’t test its controls against a live router here. The UI reports proxy-listener status separately and doesn’t treat that alone as proof the router has bootstrapped.

Next I can add an explicit I2P+ installation flow to this panel, then work toward putting the controls in Firefox Settings.
