**Title bar fix**
- The `browser.theme.native-theme` fallback is now pinned off in [synapse.js](overlay/browser/app/profile/synapse.js), so the native system titlebar material (that light mauve strip) can't take over the top row.
- The stylesheet also explicitly forces `appearance: none` on the titlebar backdrop and paints the titlebar rows with the chrome surface color, so the strip behind the traffic lights is the same near-black as the nav bar below it — in both Light and Dark system appearances.
- This also fixes the white "selected tab" effect you had: tab colors no longer follow `light-dark()` system switching.

**Krypton palette conversion** (from krypton-lang.org + kryptonbytes.com)
- Surfaces: `#0a0a0f` title bar, `#0f0f17` toolbars, `#0b0b15` URL field, `#1a1a26` cards/selected tab — KryptonBytes' own surface stack.
- Accent: Krypton violet `#7722ff` for focus outlines, field focus border, separators, and hover/active tints (`rgb(119 34 255 / 18%)` hover).
- Text: KryptonBytes' `#f5f5fb` with `#9a9ab2` muted inactive text; links use the site's `#a974ff` violet with `#c0a0ff` hover.
- The cyan/mint from the old midnight theme is gone; it's all violet-family now.

Everything is in [synapse-theme.css](overlay/browser/themes/shared/synapse-theme.css), still uncommitted. Tell me how it looks — if the strip is still tinted, send another screenshot and I'll dig into the exact layer drawing it.
