What draws menus? XUL menubar (hidden on macOS - global menubar is native NSMenu!) — on macOS the application menu bar is NATIVE, rendered by AppKit with the system appearance (Golden Gate → warm gray). CSS can't restyle the native menu bar. But we can control the *tint* by changing the window's/appearance via NSAppearance... Firefox sets NSAppearance based on prefers-color-scheme? If the browser chrome is dark, Firefox on macOS switches the app's NSAppearance to dark, making the global menu bar dark. Currently, because our chrome is dark but the document color scheme may still be light, the menu stays light Golden Gate.

Firefox pref: `layout.css.prefers-color-scheme.content-override` = 2 (system), 1 light, 0 dark... For chrome documents, prefers-color-scheme follows the widget theme. There's a known behavior: when browser.theme content-override is set to dark, Firefox sets NSAppearanceNameDarkAqua globally, and native menu bar becomes dark.

So the ask: when Synapse window active, make global menu bar match hue (dark violet-ish). Options:
