Fixed and relaunched with zero warnings. In the fresh instance, click the chevron again — you should now see the labels in light violet-white text (`#f5f5fb`) on the Krypton panel surface (`#1a1a26`) with a subtle `#2a2a3c` border, including "Search All Tabs", "New Container Tab", "Current window", "View All Tabs", and the tab list rows.

What went wrong before, and why the hover row had no visible text:

- Gecko's panel tokens (`--panel-text-color` etc.) resolve through `light-dark()` based on the document's used color scheme. Your macOS system (Golden Gate, Light side) had panel text resolving to **near-black**, while the panel background was already dark from our Krypton overrides — dark text on a dark panel, with only the hover highlight giving away the rows.
- The `color-scheme: dark` declaration (added for the menu bar) fixes the pairing, and the new explicit panel tokens in [synapse-theme.css](overlay/browser/themes/shared/synapse-theme.css) pin the exact Krypton values so those popups never depend on the system appearance again.

All these theme changes remain uncommitted. If any other popup (right-click menu, downloads panel, etc.) has a similar legibility or color mismatch, send a screenshot and I'll extend the same treatment.
