Done. Synapse is restarted with the new defaults in place:

- **Startup** opens on `https://www.krypton-lang.org/s.html` (the Synapse start page).
- **New tabs** also open on that page by default.
- **Both are user-selectable** in Settings → Home: the "New Windows and Tabs" section natively offers Firefox Home / Blank page / **Custom URLs...**, and since our Krypton URL is a distribution default (not a lock), picking a custom URL there overrides it per profile. Anything typed in those two fields persists like any Firefox setting.

Implementation-wise it's three prefs in [synapse.js](overlay/browser/app/profile/synapse.js): `browser.startup.page=1`, `browser.startup.homepage`, and `browser.newtab.url` — this version's Settings pane can drive both fields, so no custom UI was needed. One side effect to know: because the new tab now loads a remote page, the built-in Firefox Home (tiles/activity-stream) is bypassed by default; the tiles you saw in your screenshot are still reachable by choosing "Firefox Home" in Settings → Home → New tabs.

Also still pending from the theme build running earlier: flip your system appearance Light ↔ Dark and check that the title bar/menu bar now follows it. If anything looks off on the light Krypton mode (contrast, panel text), send a screenshot and I'll tune those tokens.
